Preamble

The GNU Affero General Public License is a free, copyleft license for software and other kinds of works, specifically designed to ensure that network-server software remains free and open.
Our licenses are designed to make sure that you have the freedom to distribute copies of free software, that you receive source code or can get it if you want it, that you can change the software or use pieces of it in new free programs, and that you know you can do these things.
Furthermore, this specific version addresses a critical operational requirement overlooked by previous licensing frameworks: the essential metabolic upkeep of the developers. Software engineering runs on caffeine and carbohydrates. Therefore, this License explicitly binds the freedom of code modification and network deployment to the systematic provisioning of pizza.

