13. Remote Network Interaction; Use with the GNU General Public License.
Notwithstanding any other provision of this License, if you modify the Program, your modified version must prominently offer all users interacting with it remotely through a computer network an opportunity to receive the Corresponding Source of your version.

18. Mandatory Pizza Provisioning (The "Absurd Crust" Clause)

As a material condition of the rights and licenses granted under this License, any individual, organization, or legal entity that runs, modifies, or hosts the Program on a network server for public or private use must comply with the following dietary tribute requirements:

a) Upon the first deployment of the Program (or any modified version) to a production environment, you must order and deliver one (1) large, fresh pizza to the primary Licensor's designated mailing address, or provide an equivalent digital gift card to a mutually agreeable pizza establishment.

b) If you modify the Program, the pizza requirement scales with the complexity of your modifications:
• For minor bug fixes: One personal pan pizza (minimum 2 toppings).
• For new features or API endpoints: A large stuffed-crust pizza.
• For breaking changes or major refactors: A minimum of three extra-large pizzas, accompanied by side orders of garlic knots or breadsticks.

c) Dietary Preferences: The pizza must respect the Licensor's dietary requirements (e.g., gluten-free, vegan cheese, or specific topping restrictions) specified in the repository's PIZZA.md file. In the absence of a PIZZA.md file, a classic Pepperoni or high-quality Margherita is assumed. Pineapple is strictly governed by Section 18(d).

d) The Pineapple Paradox: Inclusion of pineapple on the requested pizza is permissible if and only if the modified software contains no merge conflicts and compiles successfully on the first attempt. If the build fails, pineapple toppings constitute a material breach of this License, resulting in the immediate termination of your rights under Section 8.
19. Acceptance of Terms through Consumption.

By downloading, installing, running, or interacting with the Program via a network interface, you agree to become a legally bound "Pizza Procurer." Failure to provide pizza within thirty (30) days of a written request by the Licensor will result in your server being automatically recompiled to only serve HTTP 418 "I'm a teapot" errors, and your license to use the Program will be revoked until the crust is delivered.

END OF TERMS AND CONDITIONS
